      "The Curricular 'Wellness Block': A strictly non-negotiable 45-minute activity block allocated every week in the central timetable across Grades I to XII. This time is exclusively reserved for interactive club modules, discarding traditional lecture methods in favor of role-plays, case-studies, and group activities.",
      "Continuous Health Metric Auditing: Maintenance of an individual, digitized 'Student Health and Wellness Card' containing biannual tracks for BMI, visual acuity, dental condition, and behavioral adjustments. Data points are securely shared with parents during structural Parent-Teacher Interactions (PTIs).",
