      "Internal Complaints Committee (ICC): The school has an Internal Complaints Committee (ICC) to receive, investigate, and address complaints of sexual harassment. The details of the committee members will be displayed prominently on the school notice board.",
      "Confidentiality: The identity of the complainant and the details of the complaint will be kept confidential to the maximum extent possible.",
      "Disciplinary Action: Any employee found guilty of sexual harassment will be subject to strict disciplinary action, which may include termination of employment.",
      "7. Termination Policy",
      "This policy outlines the procedures for the termination of employment.",
      "Resignation: An employee wishing to resign must provide written notice of at least one month for a teaching position and one month for a non-teaching position. The Principal may, at their discretion, waive or reduce the notice period.",
      "Termination by the School: Employment may be terminated by the school on grounds including, but not limited to, poor performance, misconduct, breach of policy, or redundancy. In such cases, the school will provide the employee with a written notice as per the terms of their employment contract.",
